-names></name><name><surname>Sokiranski</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Musculoskeletal involvement in cystic echinococcosis: report of eight cases and review of the literature</article-title><source>Am J Roentgenol</source><year>1997</year><volume>168</volume><fpage>1531</fpage><lpage>1534</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9168719</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>T&#x000fc;z&#x000fc;n</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hekimoglu</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CT findings in skeletal cystic echinococcosis</article-title><source>Acta Radiology</source><year>2002</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>533</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1034/j.1600-0455.2002.430515.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Madiwale</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Gary</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Chavhan</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Case report: Hydatid disease of bone</article-title><source>Australasian Radiology</source><year>2002</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>431</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12452919</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1440-1673.2002.t01-1-01099.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dalimia</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghasemikhah</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hashemi Malayeri</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Echinococcus granulosus: lethal effect of low voltage direct electric current on hydatid cyst protoscoleces</article-title><source>Experimental Parasitology</source><year>2005</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>237</fpage><lpage>240</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15755421</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.exppara.2004.12.014</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Mandell G, Bennett J, Dolin R</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Cestodes (tapeworms)</article-title><source>Principles and practices of infectious diseases</source><year>2000</year><edition>5</edition><publisher-name>New York: Churchill Livingstone</publisher-name><fpage>633</fpage><lpage>640</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lam</surname><given-names>KS</given-names></name><name><surname>Faraj</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Mulholland</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Finch</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Medical decompression of Vertebral Hydatidosis</article-title><source>Spine</source><year>1997</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>2050</fpage><lpage>2055</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9306538</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00007632-199709010-00023</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gossios</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kantoyannis</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Dascalogiannaki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gowrtsoyiannis</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Uncommon Location of hydatid disease, CT appearances</article-title><source>Eur Radiology</source><year>1997</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>1303</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s003300050293</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mattern</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gardner</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Grose</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Helfet</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Case report: Echinococcus disease of the bone presenting as a femoral shaft nonunion</article-title><source>Clin Orthop Relat Res</source><year>2007</year><volume>458</volume><fpage>220</fpage><lpage>225</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17159572</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guisantes</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Progress on the laboratory diagnosis of the human hydatid disease &#x02013; from the recent past till the present</article-title><source>Arch int Hidatid</source><year>1997</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>136</fpage><lpage>140</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Manes</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Santucci</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Echinococcosis: intramuscular localization</article-title><source>Cir Organi Mov</source><year>1990</year><volume>75</volume><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>196</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2279424</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eckert</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Schantz</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Gasser</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><name><surname>Torgerson</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name><name><surname>Bessonov</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Movsessian</surname><given-names>SO</given-names></name><name><surname>Thakur</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Grimm</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Nikogossian</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Geographic distribution and prevalence of Echinococcus granulosus</article-title><source>WHO/OIE Manual on Echinococcosis in Humans and Animals: a Public Health Problem of Global Concern: 2001; France</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Eckert J, Gemmell MA, Meslin F-X, Paw&#x00142;owski ZS</publisher-name><fpage>103</fpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>